cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Scrinalia in academic work, a report or an institutional deployment, please cite it as below."
title: "Scrinalia"
abstract: >-
  A system for archivists to catalogue and manage archival descriptions (ISAD(G) metadata) with AI
  enrichment — named-entity recognition, zero-shot classification and clustering — under
  human-in-the-loop governance. Three layers (ingestion, staging, archive) plus an identity domain,
  a curation API and a React curator interface. Installed by an institution on its own
  infrastructure, offline by design.
type: software
